/-!
# Hand proof of the smaller-short case, heavy S0 sign: outer face, `τ = 8T/9` test `F(8T/9, -1/9)`, coefficients

The outer face, `τ = 8T/9` test `F(8T/9, -1/9)` (`OUTER_SCALE_LARGE_RATIO_SIGN (7)`; inventory HS-S01 B9) as the sign of a
cleared numerator `N` in `(x, α, β)`, certified by nested Bernstein expansions: in `b = β - x` on
`[0, x(7x+1)(α-1)/(4x²+11x+1)]`, then in `a = α - α₀` on `[0, x - (22x + 20)/55]`; the resulting
coefficients are polynomials in `X = x - 12/5` with nonnegative coefficients (no bound `x ≤ 9`
needed).

Route: the notes' β-lower strip end is replaced by `β ≥ x` (the sign holds on the larger strip), and their `t`-Bernstein table by the nested certificate.

Generated by `scripts/certificates/short-hand/s0/gens0.py`; every identity is checked by
`ring`/`field_simp`, every final sign by `positivity`.

## Main API

* `hh0O8N`, `hh0O8M*`, `hh0O8c*`, `hh0O8n*`, `hh0O8e*`: the numerator and its coefficient polynomials.
* `hh0O8_L1_*`: the first level-1 signs.
-/

@[expose] public section

